\title{Tangled Hierarchies:\\ Proof Systems That Reference Their Own Soundness}
\author{Aristotle}
\date{17 August 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
We give a complete frame-theoretic account of what it costs a formal system to contain its own soundness predicate. Working in the semantics of arbitrary Kripke frames --- deliberately \emph{not} assuming well-foundedness, since well-foundedness is precisely what is at stake --- we prove that a world validates the reflection (soundness) schema $\Box\varphi\to\varphi$ uniformly in the valuation \emph{if and only if} it accesses itself. Internalised soundness \emph{is} a strange loop, in the exact sense of an edge from a vantage point to itself. Four sharpenings follow. The schema cannot be weakened: reflection for propositional variables alone already forces the loop and hence the full schema. The loop cannot be avoided but can be isolated: every frame extends, by one new top world, to a frame with an internally sound world; the extension preserves the truth of every formula at every old world, has exactly one self-loop and exactly one sound world; iterating gives a tower whose $n$-th stage has exactly $n$ sound worlds and still contains an unsound one. The loop can be stretched, not removed: a world validates the $n$-fold principle $\Box^{n}\varphi\to\varphi$ iff it lies on a closed walk of length exactly $n$; cycle frames on $n$ worlds realise degree $n$ while refuting all smaller positive degrees and having no self-loops, yet remain tangled in the transitive closure, and no provability frame admits any positive degree. Finally the boundary is at reflection, not consistency: internal consistency $\neg\Box\bot$ is seriality and is validated on a loop-free converse-well-founded chain, while every \emph{finite} frame sound for a system proving its own consistency must be tangled. At the level of proof systems we prove a trichotomy: well-founded and silent, or self-certifying and tangled --- and nothing else.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}

The standard hygiene of metamathematics is stratification. Statements about a theory live one floor above the theory; the ``is about'' relation is well founded and the tower never bends back on itself. Tarski's theorem on the undefinability of truth and G\"odel's second incompleteness theorem are the classical reasons for the discipline.

Yet the temptation to internalise self-certification is permanent. What we would like a trusted system $S$ to contain is the \textbf{reflection schema}
\[
\Box\varphi\to\varphi \qquad (\varphi \text{ any formula of } S\text{'s own language}),
\]
where $\Box$ is $S$'s provability predicate: \emph{whatever I prove is true}. Hofstadter named the resulting configuration a \textbf{tangled hierarchy}: a level structure whose higher levels reach back down into the levels they were meant to survey.

This paper asks the quantitative question. Granting that the tangle is unavoidable, \emph{how much} tangle is forced, where exactly does it appear, and can it be weakened, delayed, isolated, or paid off in instalments? We answer all four in the Kripke semantics of modal provability logic, where ``tangle'' becomes a concrete graph property: a closed walk in the accessibility relation.

\paragraph{Summary of results.}
\begin{enumerate}
\item \emph{Soundness $=$ Tangle} (Theorem~\ref{thm:soundtangle}): $w$ internally sound $\iff R\,w\,w$.
\item \emph{Atomic reflection} (Theorem~\ref{thm:atomic}): reflection for atoms alone is equivalent to the full schema.
\item \emph{L\"ob forbids the loop} (Lemma~\ref{lem:loebirr}), hence no world is both sound and L\"obian, and a frame validating both schemas everywhere is empty (Theorem~\ref{thm:semgodel}).
\item \emph{Structural destruction} (Section~\ref{sec:destroys}): no natural-number level grading, no well-founded rank of any kind, and escape from the least fixed point $\mu X.\Box X$, which we identify with the well-founded part of the frame.
\item \emph{Topological bridge} (Theorem~\ref{thm:interior}): $\Box$ is the interior operator of the Alexandrov topology iff every world is internally sound and the frame is transitive.
\item \emph{Cost is one loop} (Section~\ref{sec:cost}): the soundness extension, its truth lemma, exact counts, and non-convergence of the reflection tower.
\item \emph{The spectrum} (Section~\ref{sec:spectrum}): $n$-fold reflection $\iff$ closed walk of length $n$; cycle frames; the degree set is a submonoid of $(\mathbb{N},+)$.
\item \emph{The boundary} (Section~\ref{sec:boundary}) and \emph{the trichotomy} (Section~\ref{sec:systems}).
\end{enumerate}

\section{Definitions}

\subsection{Syntax}

Fix a set $\At$ of propositional variables. The modal language is generated by
\[
\varphi ::= p \mid \bot \mid \varphi\to\varphi \mid \Box\varphi, \qquad p\in\At .
\]
Negation is $\neg\varphi := \varphi\to\bot$ and the \textbf{consistency statement} is $\Con := \neg\Box\bot$. We write $\Refl(\varphi) := \Box\varphi\to\varphi$ for the \textbf{reflection instance} and $\Loeb(\varphi) := \Box(\Box\varphi\to\varphi)\to\Box\varphi$ for the \textbf{L\"ob instance}. The iterated box is $\Box^{0}\varphi := \varphi$, $\Box^{n+1}\varphi := \Box\,\Box^{n}\varphi$.

\subsection{Frames and satisfaction}

\begin{definition}[Frame]
A \emph{frame} is a pair $F=(W,R)$ with $W$ a set of \emph{worlds} and $R \subseteq W\times W$ the \emph{accessibility relation}. No further condition is imposed: neither transitivity, nor irreflexivity, nor well-foundedness.
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}[Satisfaction]
A \emph{valuation} is $V:\At\to\mathcal{P}(W)$. Satisfaction is defined by
\[
w\models_V p \iff w\in V(p), \qquad w\not\models_V\bot,
\]
\[
w\models_V \varphi\to\psi \iff (w\models_V\varphi \Rightarrow w\models_V\psi),
\qquad
w\models_V\Box\varphi \iff \forall v\,(R\,w\,v \Rightarrow v\models_V\varphi).
\]
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}[Provability frame]
A \emph{provability frame} is a transitive, converse well-founded frame: there is no infinite chain $w_0 R w_1 R w_2 R\cdots$. Converse well-foundedness implies irreflexivity. These are exactly the frames validating L\"ob's axiom.
\end{definition}

\begin{definition}[Internal soundness]
$w$ is \emph{internally sound} if $\forall V\,\forall\varphi:\ w\models_V \Box\varphi\to\varphi$. It is \emph{atomically sound} if this holds for all atoms $\varphi = p$. It has \emph{soundness degree $n$}, written $\IS_n(w)$, if $\forall V\,\forall\varphi:\ w\models_V \Box^{n}\varphi\to\varphi$. It \emph{validates L\"ob} if $\forall V\,\forall\varphi:\ w\models_V \Loeb(\varphi)$.
\end{definition}

The quantifier over valuations is essential: soundness is a property of the world in the frame, not of a particular interpretation.

\begin{definition}[$n$-step accessibility; tangledness]
$R^{(0)}u\,v :\iff u = v$ and $R^{(n+1)}u\,v :\iff \exists z\,(R\,u\,z \wedge R^{(n)}z\,v)$. Thus $R^{(n)}w\,w$ says $w$ lies on a \emph{closed walk of length exactly $n$}. A relation $S$ is \emph{tangled} if $S\,a\,b$ and $S\,b\,a$ for some $a,b$ (possibly equal); a tangled relation admits no \emph{grading}, i.e.\ no $\rank : W\to\mathbb{N}$ with $S\,a\,b\Rightarrow \rank(a)<\rank(b)$.
\end{definition}

\section{Internalised soundness is exactly a self-loop}

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:loopsound}
If $R\,w\,w$ then $w$ is internally sound.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}
If $w\models_V\Box\varphi$ then $\varphi$ holds at every successor of $w$, and $w$ is one of them.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Soundness $=$ Tangle]\label{thm:soundtangle}
For every frame and world, $w$ is internally sound if and only if $R\,w\,w$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
($\Leftarrow$) is Lemma~\ref{lem:loopsound}. For ($\Rightarrow$), fix an atom $p$ and define the \emph{diagonal valuation} $V^{\ast}(p) := \{v : R\,w\,v\}$. By construction $p$ holds at every successor of $w$, so $w\models_{V^{\ast}}\Box p$. The instance $\Box p\to p$ gives $w\models_{V^{\ast}}p$, i.e.\ $R\,w\,w$.
\end{proof}

\begin{remark}
The theorem needs the quantifier over valuations; relative to a fixed valuation an irreflexive world can be accidentally sound (see Section~\ref{sec:systems}).
\end{remark}

\begin{theorem}[No safe fragment]\label{thm:atomic}
A world is atomically sound if and only if it is internally sound.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
One direction is trivial. Conversely, the diagonal valuation uses only an atomic instance, so atomic soundness gives $R\,w\,w$, and Lemma~\ref{lem:loopsound} upgrades this to the full schema.
\end{proof}

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:loebirr}
If $w$ validates L\"ob then $\neg R\,w\,w$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
Take a valuation making an atom $p$ false everywhere and consider $\Loeb(p)$. A self-loop at $w$ makes $\Box(\Box p\to p)$ true at $w$, whence $\Box p$, whence $p$ at $w$ by the loop --- contradicting the choice of valuation.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Semantic second incompleteness]\label{thm:semgodel}
No world is both internally sound and L\"ob-validating. A frame in which every world validates both schemas is empty. In particular no world of a provability frame is internally sound.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Combine Theorem~\ref{thm:soundtangle} with Lemma~\ref{lem:loebirr}; provability frames are irreflexive.
\end{proof}

\section{What the tangle destroys}\label{sec:destroys}

\begin{theorem}\label{thm:nolevels}
If a frame has an internally sound world then $R$ is tangled, and there is no $\rank : W\to\mathbb{N}$ with $R\,a\,b\Rightarrow\rank(a)<\rank(b)$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Absoluteness of the collapse]
If $w$ is internally sound then for no well-founded relation $s$ on any set $B$ is there $\rho:W\to B$ with $R\,a\,b\Rightarrow s\,\rho(b)\,\rho(a)$; in particular no ordinal-valued grading exists.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Such a $\rho$ would give $s\,\rho(w)\,\rho(w)$, impossible in a well-founded relation.
\end{proof}

\subsection{Box as a set operator}

For $X\subseteq W$ put $\Box X := \{w : \forall v\,(R\,w\,v\Rightarrow v\in X)\}$. This is monotone, so $\mu X.\Box X$ exists by Knaster--Tarski.

\begin{theorem}
$\mu X.\Box X$ is exactly the well-founded part of $R$, i.e.\ the set of worlds accessible for the converse relation.
\end{theorem}

\begin{theorem}[L\"ob's principle as induction]
The following are equivalent: (i) for all $X$, $\Box X\subseteq X$ implies $X=W$; (ii) $\mu X.\Box X = W$; (iii) $R$ is converse well founded.
\end{theorem}

\begin{corollary}
If $R\,w\,w$ then $w\notin\mu X.\Box X$, hence $\mu X.\Box X\neq W$: an internally sound world escapes every L\"ob-style induction.
\end{corollary}

\subsection{The topological bridge}

A frame carries its \emph{Alexandrov topology}: $X$ is open iff it is closed under accessibility.

\begin{theorem}[Interior $=$ provability iff everywhere sound and transitive]\label{thm:interior}
For a frame $F$ the following are equivalent: (i) $\operatorname{int}(X) = \Box X$ for every $X\subseteq W$; (ii) every world of $F$ is internally sound and $R$ is transitive.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
(ii)$\Rightarrow$(i): soundness everywhere gives reflexivity, so $\Box X\subseteq X$; transitivity makes $\Box X$ open; any open $U\subseteq X$ satisfies $U\subseteq\Box X$; hence $\Box X$ is the largest open subset of $X$. (i)$\Rightarrow$(ii): from $\Box X\subseteq X$ for all $X$, applied to $X = \{v : R\,w\,v\}$, we get $R\,w\,w$; idempotence $\Box X\subseteq\Box\Box X$ applied to the same set gives transitivity.
\end{proof}

\begin{corollary}
On a nonempty provability frame, $\Box$ is never the interior operator of the Alexandrov topology.
\end{corollary}

\section{The cost is exactly one loop}\label{sec:cost}

\begin{definition}[Soundness extension]
For $F=(W,R)$ let $F^{+}$ have worlds $W\sqcup\{\top\}$ with $R^{+}\top x$ for all $x$ including $\top$; $R^{+}u\,v \iff R\,u\,v$ for $u,v\in W$; and $\neg R^{+}u\,\top$ for $u\in W$.
\end{definition}

\begin{theorem}[Truth lemma; conservation]\label{thm:truthlemma}
Extend a valuation to $F^{+}$ by making every atom false at $\top$. Then for every formula $\varphi$ and every old world $v$: $v\models^{F^{+}}\varphi$ iff $v\models^{F}\varphi$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
Induction on $\varphi$; the $\Box$ case is exactly the statement that $W$ is a generated submodel, since no old world accesses $\top$.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Exact cost]\label{thm:exactcost}
$\top$ is internally sound in $F^{+}$. If $F$ is irreflexive then $\top$ is the unique self-accessing and the unique internally sound world of $F^{+}$; moreover $F^{+}$ fails converse well-foundedness exactly at $\top$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{corollary}
For every provability frame $M$: no world of $M$ is internally sound; $M$ embeds into $M^{+}$ preserving all truths at old worlds; $M^{+}$ has a unique internally sound world; and $M^{+}$ admits no natural-number grading.
\end{corollary}

\begin{definition}[Reflection tower]
$F^{(0)} := F$ and $F^{(n+1)} := (F^{(n)})^{+}$: stage $n+1$ reasons about, and certifies the soundness of, stage $n$.
\end{definition}

\begin{theorem}[One loop per stage]\label{thm:onelooop}
If $F$ is irreflexive then the self-accessing worlds of $F^{(n)}$ form a finite set of cardinality exactly $n$; equivalently $F^{(n)}$ has exactly $n$ internally sound worlds, however large $F$ is.
\end{theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Non-convergence]\label{thm:nonconv}
If $F$ is irreflexive and nonempty then every stage $F^{(n)}$ still contains a world that is not internally sound.
\end{theorem}

\begin{corollary}
For a nonempty provability frame $M$ and any $n$: stage $n$ has exactly $n$ internally sound worlds, still has an unsound world, and every sound world of stage $n+1$ lies outside $\mu X.\Box X$ and admits no ordinal grading.
\end{corollary}

\section{The spectrum of tangles}\label{sec:spectrum}

\begin{lemma}\label{lem:boxiter}
$w\models_V \Box^{n}\varphi$ iff $\varphi$ holds at every $v$ with $R^{(n)}w\,v$.
\end{lemma}

\begin{theorem}[Spectrum Theorem]\label{thm:spectrum}
For every frame, world $w$ and $n\in\mathbb{N}$: $\IS_n(w) \iff R^{(n)}w\,w$. That is, $w$ validates $\Box^{n}\varphi\to\varphi$ uniformly in the valuation iff $w$ lies on a closed walk of length exactly $n$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
($\Leftarrow$) by Lemma~\ref{lem:boxiter}. ($\Rightarrow$) diagonalise at distance $n$: interpret an atom $p$ as $\{v : R^{(n)}w\,v\}$; then $w\models\Box^{n}p$, so the instance $\Box^{n}p\to p$ gives $R^{(n)}w\,w$.
\end{proof}

\begin{proposition}[Degrees form a monoid]
$\IS_0(w)$ always holds, and $\IS_m(w)$ together with $\IS_n(w)$ implies $\IS_{m+n}(w)$. Hence the \emph{soundness spectrum} $D(w) := \{n : \IS_n(w)\}$ is a submonoid of $(\mathbb{N},+)$.
\end{proposition}

\begin{proof}
Degree $0$ is $\varphi\to\varphi$; addition is concatenation of closed walks, via Theorem~\ref{thm:spectrum}.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}
If $\IS_n(w)$ for some $n\ge 1$ then the transitive closure of $R$ is tangled and admits no natural-number grading. On a transitive frame, $R^{(n)}u\,v$ with $n \ge 1$ implies $R\,u\,v$; consequently no world of a provability frame has any positive soundness degree.
\end{theorem}

\begin{definition}[Cycle frame]
$C_n$ has worlds $\mathbb{Z}/n\mathbb{Z}$ and $R\,i\,j \iff j = i+1$. In $C_n$, $R^{(k)}i\,j$ iff $j = i+k \pmod n$.
\end{definition}

\begin{theorem}[Degree exactly $n$]\label{thm:cycle}
For $n\ge 2$: every world of $C_n$ validates $\Box^{n}\varphi\to\varphi$; no world validates $\Box^{k}\varphi\to\varphi$ for $0<k<n$; no world accesses itself; and the transitive closure of the accessibility relation is nevertheless tangled.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
$i+n\equiv i$ gives the first claim. For the second, $\IS_k(i)$ would give $n \mid k$, impossible for $0<k<n$; taking $k=1$ gives loop-freeness. Tangledness follows from the closed walk of length $n$.
\end{proof}

Thus internal soundness comes in a strictly increasing hierarchy of tangle lengths: delayed self-trust is genuinely available and genuinely spread across $n$ levels, but the closed walk itself cannot be removed.

\section{Where the boundary lies: consistency is free}\label{sec:boundary}

\begin{theorem}
For every frame, valuation and world: $w\models\Con$ iff $w$ has at least one successor. In particular internal consistency does not depend on the valuation.
\end{theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Consistency costs nothing]
The two-world chain $t\to f$ is loop-free and converse well founded, yet $t$ satisfies $\Con$ under every valuation; and $t$ is not internally sound, not even atomically.
\end{theorem}

\begin{corollary}
Internal consistency is compatible with a converse-well-founded, loop-free frame; internal soundness of any positive degree is not. The jump from untangled to tangled happens exactly at reflection.
\end{corollary}

\begin{definition}[Modal proof system]
A \emph{modal proof system} is a set $\Thm$ of formulas closed under modus ponens and necessitation. It is \emph{consistent} if $\bot\notin\Thm$, and \emph{frame-sound for $F$} if every theorem holds at every world of $F$ under every valuation.
\end{definition}

\begin{theorem}
If $S$ proves $\Con$ and $F$ is frame-sound for $S$ then $F$ is serial. Hence a converse-well-founded such $F$ is empty; in particular no nonempty provability frame is sound for a system proving its own consistency.
\end{theorem}

\begin{lemma}
A finite nonempty serial frame contains a world lying on a cycle of its transitive closure.
\end{lemma}

\begin{proof}[Proof sketch]
Choose a successor function $f$ and iterate from any world; by finiteness $f^{i}(w) = f^{j}(w)$ for some $i<j$, giving a closed walk of positive length.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}[Unavoidability, finite case]
Every finite nonempty frame sound for a proof system asserting its own consistency has a tangled transitive closure, hence admits no natural-number grading.
\end{theorem}

\begin{theorem}[Sharpness]
Finiteness cannot be dropped: the $\omega$-chain $0\to1\to2\to\cdots$ is serial and loop-free even in its transitive closure.
\end{theorem}

\section{Proof systems: the trichotomy}\label{sec:systems}

\begin{theorem}[L\"ob's rule]
In a system proving the L\"ob axiom, if $\Box\varphi\to\varphi$ is a theorem then so is $\varphi$.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Necessitation gives $\Box(\Box\varphi\to\varphi)$; the L\"ob axiom and modus ponens give $\Box\varphi$; the hypothesis gives $\varphi$.
\end{proof}

\begin{theorem}
A system proving the L\"ob axiom and containing its own soundness predicate is inconsistent.
\end{theorem}

\begin{proof}
Apply L\"ob's rule with $\varphi=\bot$.
\end{proof}

\begin{corollary}[Second incompleteness, modally]
A consistent L\"obian system proves neither $\Con$ nor any complete soundness schema; conversely a consistent system containing its own soundness predicate cannot be L\"obian.
\end{corollary}

\paragraph{Two concrete systems.} Let the \emph{well-founded system} have as theorems the formulas valid at every world of every provability frame. It is closed under modus ponens and necessitation, is L\"obian, and is consistent (witness: the one-point irreflexive frame). Let the \emph{tangled system} have as theorems the formulas true under every valuation at the world of the one-point reflexive frame. It is closed under the same rules, proves every reflection instance, proves $\Con$, and is consistent; hence it must refute the L\"ob axiom.

\begin{theorem}[Trichotomy]
For every propositional signature:
\begin{enumerate}
\item the well-founded system is consistent, proves every instance of the L\"ob axiom, and does not contain its own soundness predicate;
\item the tangled system is consistent, contains its own soundness predicate and proves its own consistency statement, and does not prove the L\"ob axiom;
\item no modal proof system whatsoever is simultaneously consistent, L\"obian, and in possession of its own soundness predicate.
\end{enumerate}
\end{theorem}

\paragraph{A genuine internal soundness predicate.} Tangling is not the only phenomenon available. On the two-world frame $\{f,t\}$ in which both worlds access $t$ and only $t$, the valuation $V(s) := \{t\}$ makes $s$ hold at exactly the worlds sound relative to $V$: a genuine modal fixed point, non-vacuous since $t$ is sound and $f$ is not. Naming your soundness is safe; asserting it at every world forces seriality, and a converse-well-founded frame realising that is empty.

\section{Algorithms}

\begin{algorithmbox}[Soundness spectrum of a world]
Given a finite frame with $N$ worlds and a world $w$, compute $\{n \le K : \IS_n(w)\} = \{n\le K : R^{(n)}w\,w\}$ by iterating the frontier $S_{n+1} = R[S_n]$ from $S_0 = \{w\}$: time $O(K\cdot|R|)$, space $O(N)$.
\end{algorithmbox}

\begin{algorithmbox}[Sound-world census and tangle test]
Compute $\{w : R\,w\,w\}$ in $O(N)$ and the transitive closure in $O(N\cdot|R|)$; a diagonal entry certifies tangledness and hence, by Theorem~\ref{thm:nolevels}, that no grading exists. If there is none, a grading is produced by topological sort in $O(N+|R|)$.
\end{algorithmbox}

\begin{algorithmbox}[Reflection tower simulation]
Apply the soundness extension $n$ times to an irreflexive frame; the loop count at stage $n$ is exactly $n$ and at least one world remains unsound, both verified in $O(N+n)$ per stage.
\end{algorithmbox}

\section{Discussion}

Self-certification is a graph property: uniform internal soundness of degree $n$ is \emph{identical} to lying on a closed walk of length $n$, so every semantic question about internalised soundness reduces to reachability. It has no weak fragments, only slow ones: atomic reflection already yields the whole schema, while $n$-fold reflection stratifies into a strictly increasing hierarchy realised by cycle frames. It is conservative where it matters: the minimal tangling changes no truth of the original hierarchy, costs exactly one loop and yields exactly one sound world. It cannot be reached by stratification: every finite stage of the reflection tower has an unsound world. And it is a property of soundness, not coherence: consistency is seriality and is free on well-founded frames, becoming unavoidable only under finiteness.

Theorem~\ref{thm:interior} adds a cross-domain reading: the S4/interior semantics of $\Box$ is \emph{equivalent} to universal internal soundness plus transitivity, so the choice between the ``provability'' and ``interior'' readings of the same symbol is exactly the choice between well-foundedness and self-trust.

The framework is deliberately austere --- propositional modal language, no arithmetic, no coding --- so the results are statements about reference structure rather than arithmetical strength. Bridging to arithmetised provability, where the correspondence with frames is the arithmetical completeness theory of provability logic, would turn the frame-level costing into a costing in terms of theories and reflection principles.

\section{Future work}

\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{The soundness-degree monoid.} $D(w)$ is a submonoid of $(\mathbb{N},+)$ equal to $\{0\}$ exactly when $w$ lies on no cycle, and cycle frames realise the principal submonoids $n\mathbb{N}$. Conjecture: every submonoid arises as some $D(w)$, making self-soundness a complete numerical-semigroup invariant.
\item \textbf{Global conservativity.} Conjecture: the soundness extension is conservative for global consequence, and so is the direct limit of the reflection tower.
\item \textbf{A topological trichotomy.} Classify frames by the behaviour of $\Box$ relative to the interior operator; the two extremes are pinned by Theorem~\ref{thm:interior} and the intermediate class is unexplored.
\item \textbf{Degrees beyond $\omega$.} Transfinite reflection towers and ordinal-indexed reflection principles.
\item \textbf{Arithmetical realisation.} Which frame phenomena are realised by concrete theories with concrete reflection principles?
\end{enumerate}

\section{Conclusion}

Internalised soundness is not a subtle syntactic condition; it is a loop, and only a loop. A world trusts itself exactly when it sees itself, and trusts itself with an $n$-step delay exactly when it lies on a closed walk of $n$ steps. This identification converts the subject into graph theory, and every structural consequence follows: no levels, no ordinal ranks, no L\"ob induction, no coexistence with the well-founded provability discipline, no non-trivial safe fragment, no convergence of stratification. In compensation the loop is cheap and clean --- one edge, one world, no disturbance to any pre-existing truth --- and it is the price of soundness alone. Tangled hierarchies are neither pathologies nor accidents: they are the exact and minimal shape that self-certification must take.

\end{document}

